1
00:00:00,027 --> 00:00:02,720
Qwen 27B is one of the best
models you can run

2
00:00:02,786 --> 00:00:06,110
on your own machine:
more than 6 million downloads in a month.

3
00:00:06,485 --> 00:00:09,491
Except that if you want to do more
than ask it about the weather,

4
00:00:09,612 --> 00:00:11,394
it needs room for your conversation.

5
00:00:11,818 --> 00:00:13,845
To be comfortable: 32 GB of VRAM.

6
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,574
And in 2026, VRAM is gold.

7
00:00:16,949 --> 00:00:19,354
Those 32 GB can cost you €2,800…

8
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:21,155
or, if you're smart, a lot less.

9
00:00:21,874 --> 00:00:24,430
So, which route to 32 GB do you take,

10
00:00:24,537 --> 00:00:25,926
and what trap is it hiding?

11
00:00:26,299 --> 00:00:30,140
In this video, we'll see how much
memory Qwen 27B really takes.

12
00:00:30,578 --> 00:00:32,744
Then, 3 routes to 32 GB,

13
00:00:32,852 --> 00:00:36,458
with the best prices I found
on November 20, and the trap in each one.

14
00:00:36,926 --> 00:00:40,291
The same card, €400 more expensive
depending on the site you click,

15
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:43,898
and a whole computer cheaper
than a 32 GB card in stock.

16
00:00:44,339 --> 00:00:46,812
And at the end, the route I'd
take depending on your PC.

17
00:00:47,393 --> 00:00:50,138
First answer, and it might
already save you a card:

18
00:00:50,392 --> 00:00:52,327
for Qwen 27B at 4 bits,

19
00:00:52,347 --> 00:00:55,393
with a short conversation,
24 GB is enough.

20
00:00:55,886 --> 00:00:59,009
So the 32 is, really,
to give it a long memory.

21
00:00:59,357 --> 00:01:00,750
Because while you're chatting,

22
00:01:00,803 --> 00:01:02,793
the model keeps notes
on everything that's been said.

23
00:01:03,175 --> 00:01:04,554
Your file, though, doesn't change.

24
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:07,665
But those notes grow with every message.

25
00:01:08,093 --> 00:01:09,303
And we can calculate them,

26
00:01:09,432 --> 00:01:11,568
from the model's official configuration.

27
00:01:11,959 --> 00:01:16,098
With a 16-bit cache,
it's about 2 GB for 32,000 tokens,

28
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:20,703
8 for 128,000,
and 16 for the full window of 262,000.

29
00:01:21,141 --> 00:01:22,431
So do the math with me.

30
00:01:22,858 --> 00:01:26,912
The 4-bit file is 16.5 GB on Hugging Face.

31
00:01:27,349 --> 00:01:29,887
But counted the way your card
counts it, it's a bit over 15.

32
00:01:30,317 --> 00:01:32,228
You add 16 for the full conversation.

33
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:34,376
That makes 31.4.

34
00:01:34,869 --> 00:01:36,039
On a 32 GB card.

35
00:01:36,467 --> 00:01:38,935
And that's before buffers
and everything else the engine needs.

36
00:01:39,336 --> 00:01:42,592
Well, the box says 32 GB,
but your margin is already gone.

37
00:01:43,013 --> 00:01:47,062
So with 32 GB,
the full context has to be earned:

38
00:01:47,296 --> 00:01:50,487
by compressing the cache,
or by shortening the conversation a bit.

39
00:01:50,909 --> 00:01:54,055
And if you only have an 8 GB card,
we saw in a previous video

40
00:01:54,075 --> 00:01:57,499
how Qwen 27B still runs
on it, just by changing the file.

41
00:01:57,902 --> 00:01:59,532
Here, we're talking about
people who want the room.

42
00:02:00,169 --> 00:02:04,620
First route, the most tempting:
2 cards of 16 GB, and boom, 32.

43
00:02:04,937 --> 00:02:08,421
Take the RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB, the ASUS Dual.

44
00:02:09,023 --> 00:02:12,364
On November 20, on Amazon,
it was €800, in stock.

45
00:02:12,707 --> 00:02:15,357
So €1,600 for the pair,
with no limit shown on the page.

46
00:02:15,815 --> 00:02:19,929
At LDLC, the same model was €1,080,
with a little line

47
00:02:19,949 --> 00:02:22,640
above the cart button:
limited to one per customer.

48
00:02:23,102 --> 00:02:26,527
€280 more for the same model,
the same day.

49
00:02:26,941 --> 00:02:29,493
Basically, the final boss
is the site you click.

50
00:02:29,898 --> 00:02:30,648
And at AMD?

51
00:02:31,216 --> 00:02:35,752
The ASUS Radeon RX 9060 XT 16 GB was €700

52
00:02:35,772 --> 00:02:38,068
on Amazon, so €1,400 for the pair.

53
00:02:38,441 --> 00:02:39,610
Cheaper, but that day,

54
00:02:39,726 --> 00:02:42,100
delivery was announced for January 3 to 5.

55
00:02:42,479 --> 00:02:43,950
In short: Christmas without cards.

56
00:02:44,386 --> 00:02:46,601
The Intel Arc A770?

57
00:02:47,026 --> 00:02:50,305
€460 at LDLC, but out of stock online.

58
00:02:50,682 --> 00:02:53,794
And used, a 5060 Ti 16 GB

59
00:02:53,814 --> 00:02:56,582
was going for €600 to €670.

60
00:02:57,020 --> 00:03:00,067
Between individuals, though:
keep that in mind for later.

61
00:03:00,475 --> 00:03:02,613
Now, the real trap
of this route is your tower.

62
00:03:03,003 --> 00:03:06,356
Take mine: a micro-ATX motherboard,
like many others.

63
00:03:06,702 --> 00:03:09,943
According to its manual,
the second slot is as long as the first.

64
00:03:10,348 --> 00:03:14,125
Yet it only has 4 lanes of PCIe 3.0,
and it goes through the chipset.

65
00:03:14,453 --> 00:03:15,930
And on top of that, it's all
the way at the bottom.

66
00:03:16,207 --> 00:03:19,606
So a 2-slot card in there
hangs below the motherboard,

67
00:03:19,669 --> 00:03:21,899
and you need a case
with 5 expansion slots.

68
00:03:22,206 --> 00:03:26,974
And the 5060 Ti and 9060 XT
from my list are thicker:

69
00:03:27,217 --> 00:03:30,147
2.5 slots, so measure the space
under your motherboard.

70
00:03:30,527 --> 00:03:32,004
Next, the power supply.

71
00:03:32,442 --> 00:03:33,445
Mine is 1,000 watts.

72
00:03:33,465 --> 00:03:36,035
Except that with my RTX 5080 plugged in,

73
00:03:36,117 --> 00:03:38,426
I might only have 2 8-pin connectors left.

74
00:03:38,829 --> 00:03:40,507
So before buying the second card,

75
00:03:40,572 --> 00:03:42,906
you check your case,
and you count your cables.

76
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,222
And the last trap is speed.

77
00:03:45,697 --> 00:03:47,866
By default, llama.cpp splits
the model into slices of layers,

78
00:03:47,886 --> 00:03:50,027
one slice per card.

79
00:03:50,404 --> 00:03:53,465
For a single conversation,
they work one after the other.

80
00:03:53,883 --> 00:03:57,555
In fact, the memory adds up,
but the speed doesn't double.

81
00:03:57,944 --> 00:04:00,792
In short, 2 cards are about room,
not speed.

82
00:04:01,161 --> 00:04:03,475
If this video saved
you from a bad purchase, subscribe.

83
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:06,528
Second route: a single 32 GB card.

84
00:04:06,884 --> 00:04:09,717
No second slot, and suddenly
the PC is simple again.

85
00:04:10,165 --> 00:04:12,495
On November 20,
the cheapest in stock on my list

86
00:04:12,658 --> 00:04:17,329
was the ASRock Intel Arc Pro B65:
€1,900 at LDLC.

87
00:04:17,842 --> 00:04:23,008
On Amazon, B65s from third-party sellers
went down to €1,483,

88
00:04:23,101 --> 00:04:24,371
but delivered in December.

89
00:04:24,844 --> 00:04:30,051
Its bigger sister, the ASUS B70,
was €2,016 on Amazon, in stock.

90
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:34,533
On the AMD side,
the Gigabyte Radeon AI PRO R9700:

91
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:36,410
€2,400 on Amazon.

92
00:04:36,888 --> 00:04:40,659
And at LDLC,
the exact same reference: €2,800.

93
00:04:41,057 --> 00:04:43,107
So, what do those extra €400 buy you?

94
00:04:43,715 --> 00:04:45,291
Nothing. It's the same card.

95
00:04:45,674 --> 00:04:50,127
So the real match is Intel at €1,900
against AMD at €2,400.

96
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:53,220
And €500 more doesn't buy
you one more gigabyte.

97
00:04:53,618 --> 00:04:55,881
On the AMD side, I found an official guide

98
00:04:55,901 --> 00:04:59,560
to run its AI tools on the R9700.

99
00:04:59,918 --> 00:05:01,900
But 32 GB and a guide don't prove

100
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,649
that every engine supports it.

101
00:05:04,013 --> 00:05:06,179
So here's the real trap of this route:

102
00:05:06,559 --> 00:05:09,645
before comparing prices, check
that your software supports the card.

103
00:05:09,983 --> 00:05:10,733
And at NVIDIA?

104
00:05:11,171 --> 00:05:14,255
The RTX 5090 also has 32 GB.

105
00:05:14,655 --> 00:05:16,895
On Amazon, it was almost €7,000,

106
00:05:16,915 --> 00:05:19,139
from a third-party seller,
delivered late December.

107
00:05:19,508 --> 00:05:22,577
And at LDLC, €9,400, out of stock.

108
00:05:22,970 --> 00:05:25,351
At that price,
we're in a different category altogether.

109
00:05:25,774 --> 00:05:28,781
That leaves the used
Tesla V100 with 32 GB.

110
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,731
No verifiable offer in my list,
so no price.

111
00:05:32,127 --> 00:05:35,913
But its trap is a known one:
NVIDIA made the 580 driver

112
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:39,549
the last branch that supports
it, and CUDA 13 no longer compiles for it.

113
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:41,865
On top of that, like other server cards,

114
00:05:41,915 --> 00:05:45,682
it has no fan and no video output:
everything has to be redone around it.

115
00:05:46,232 --> 00:05:49,518
In fact, it can look cheap,
and cost you a whole weekend.

116
00:05:50,133 --> 00:05:52,397
Third route: change computers altogether.

117
00:05:52,835 --> 00:05:55,748
The Mac mini M6 with 32 GB
of unified memory

118
00:05:55,946 --> 00:06:01,100
and 512 of storage was listed
at €1,709 at LDLC on November 20.

119
00:06:01,517 --> 00:06:04,139
So a complete computer cost less than any

120
00:06:04,159 --> 00:06:06,711
32 GB card in stock on my list.

121
00:06:07,146 --> 00:06:10,683
First catch: it wasn't in stock
for more than 15 days.

122
00:06:11,127 --> 00:06:12,447
And if you accept waiting,

123
00:06:12,585 --> 00:06:16,737
a B65 from a third-party seller
went down to €1,483.

124
00:06:17,115 --> 00:06:18,815
And above all, this memory is shared:

125
00:06:18,835 --> 00:06:20,665
the system and your apps use it too.

126
00:06:21,052 --> 00:06:24,309
On the PC side,
there are the Ryzen AI Max+ mini PCs,

127
00:06:24,462 --> 00:06:28,019
with 64 or even 128 GB of shared memory.

128
00:06:28,502 --> 00:06:30,972
The one I looked at was around €2,000

129
00:06:31,015 --> 00:06:33,059
for 64 GB, on preorder.

130
00:06:33,476 --> 00:06:36,114
Only, its page doesn't clearly
say whether VAT is included.

131
00:06:36,502 --> 00:06:38,405
And its memory is fixed, forever.

132
00:06:38,853 --> 00:06:41,052
So the trap of this route is the bill:

133
00:06:41,231 --> 00:06:42,692
you're replacing your whole PC.

134
00:06:43,289 --> 00:06:45,959
And before paying, one last trap,
and it isn't technical.

135
00:06:46,396 --> 00:06:49,522
In France, from a professional
seller, new or used,

136
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:53,001
you get a 2-year legal guarantee,
and they can't shorten it.

137
00:06:53,399 --> 00:06:56,238
The defect is presumed to have existed
at the time of sale for those 2 years

138
00:06:56,258 --> 00:06:58,521
for new items,
and 12 months for used ones.

139
00:06:58,969 --> 00:07:00,179
And for a distance purchase,

140
00:07:00,238 --> 00:07:02,806
you have 14 days after
receiving it to withdraw.

141
00:07:03,221 --> 00:07:06,422
So those 14 days are your window
to test the card.

142
00:07:06,778 --> 00:07:09,478
But between individuals,
like on leboncoin,

143
00:07:09,602 --> 00:07:12,072
no right of withdrawal,
no legal guarantee:

144
00:07:12,255 --> 00:07:15,098
you're left with hidden defects
only, and it's up to you to prove them.

145
00:07:15,551 --> 00:07:19,157
So your used 5060 Ti,
you see it running before you pay.

146
00:07:19,552 --> 00:07:23,078
If you're watching from another country,
these prices are French prices,

147
00:07:23,098 --> 00:07:25,622
and guarantees that apply
in France and in Europe.

148
00:07:25,852 --> 00:07:28,448
Check which ones apply where you are
before you buy.

149
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,331
But the memory math,
the slots and the power supply,

150
00:07:30,351 --> 00:07:32,847
those apply everywhere.

151
00:07:33,655 --> 00:07:34,528
So, which route?

152
00:07:34,548 --> 00:07:35,778
It depends on what you already have.

153
00:07:36,246 --> 00:07:37,808
And the prices are the ones
from November 20.

154
00:07:38,259 --> 00:07:39,889
If you already have a 16 GB NVIDIA card,

155
00:07:40,066 --> 00:07:43,714
and room for another, add a 5060 Ti 16 GB:

156
00:07:43,952 --> 00:07:48,290
€800 new on Amazon,
or around €600 to €670 used.

157
00:07:48,738 --> 00:07:50,868
Half of your 32 GB is already paid for.

158
00:07:51,325 --> 00:07:54,348
If you don't have a card yet,
and your tower takes 2,

159
00:07:54,458 --> 00:07:58,236
the pair of 5060 Ti
at €1,600 was the cheapest

160
00:07:58,256 --> 00:08:00,747
path to 32 GB in stock.

161
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,811
With all the traps of the route:

162
00:08:02,901 --> 00:08:05,693
the space, the cables,
and a speed that doesn't double.

163
00:08:06,178 --> 00:08:09,886
The pair of 9060 XT cost less,
but arrived in January.

164
00:08:10,328 --> 00:08:12,474
For a single card,
I'd take the cheapest in stock:

165
00:08:12,647 --> 00:08:15,788
the B65, at €1,900 at LDLC.

166
00:08:16,246 --> 00:08:19,036
Just look at its power connector,
a 12V-2x6:

167
00:08:19,334 --> 00:08:21,392
you need that cable, or an adapter.

168
00:08:21,785 --> 00:08:26,312
If you prefer Amazon, its bigger sister,
the B70, was €2,016, in stock.

169
00:08:26,692 --> 00:08:29,477
And in every case, check
that your software supports the card.

170
00:08:29,925 --> 00:08:33,704
If it doesn't support Intel,
look at the Gigabyte R9700:

171
00:08:33,931 --> 00:08:37,058
€2,400 on Amazon, not €2,800.

172
00:08:37,481 --> 00:08:39,291
If you want to replace the whole computer,

173
00:08:39,389 --> 00:08:42,575
the Mac mini at €1,709 is in the running.

174
00:08:42,987 --> 00:08:44,788
But remember the math from the start:

175
00:08:45,001 --> 00:08:48,197
31.4 GB for the full conversation.

176
00:08:48,685 --> 00:08:52,574
On a 32 GB Mac, where the system
takes its share, with a 16-bit cache,

177
00:08:52,594 --> 00:08:55,417
it doesn't fit: you compress
the cache, or you shorten it.

178
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:58,438
And if it's really
the full conversation you want,

179
00:08:58,521 --> 00:09:01,752
the only priced route
in my list that goes past 32 GB,

180
00:09:01,772 --> 00:09:06,442
is the Ryzen AI Max+ mini PC
with 64, around €2,000.

181
00:09:06,825 --> 00:09:08,581
And actually, if you already have 24 GB

182
00:09:08,601 --> 00:09:11,308
and a short conversation is enough
for you, keep your money.

183
00:09:11,861 --> 00:09:14,240
The best card, sometimes,
is the one you don't buy.

184
00:09:14,742 --> 00:09:16,996
See you next time, bye!
